// PLACEHOLDER — this file is overwritten by the installer.
//
// It exists, and it is committed, for one reason: config.kdl does
//
//     include "cfg/output.kdl"
//
// unconditionally, because niri has no "include if it exists". A missing file
// there is a hard config error, so a fresh clone would have a broken niri
// config until the installer had run. This placeholder makes the config valid
// immediately, and contains no output block at all — so niri auto-detects your
// displays using its own EDID logic.
//
// ./install.sh   writes the real one from `niri msg outputs`
// ./regenerate.sh  rewrites it after a monitor, resolution or scale change
//
// Monitor connector names, modes, scale factors and positions are properties of
// the hardware plugged in right now. Committing them would hard-code one
// machine's monitor setup, so they are generated per host and never committed.
// This comment-only placeholder is what ships instead.

